# pytest 9.2 stores node IDs in a structured form, so pytest-xdist 3.8 cannot add
# the @group suffix: the xdist groups split and the CI shard merge gate fails.
# Remove the cap when a pytest-xdist release supports pytest 9.2. That release
# drops the @group suffix, so tools/qa_core_shards.py must change in the same
# pull request (see "Dependency updates" in AGENTS.md).
